description:
Bootle Leisure Centre was first opened in 1996 and is a well-used facility comprising a swimming pool, water slide, gym, fitness suite and sports hall.

The building is approaching 30 years old and now requires a programme of major maintenance to ensure its continued longevity and reliable operation. In 2024, Sefton Council, as owner and operator, commissioned a building survey from Mott MacDonald which identified the need for specific building maintenance operations within the children&#039;s pool area. These include:

• Maintenance painting of structural steelworks;
• Replacement of balustrades and safety railings;
• Concrete repairs and cathodic protection;
• Repairs to tiled surfaces;
• Some M&amp;E replacement and upgrading
• Drainage System Upgrade
• Replacement of Air Handling Units( separate concurrent contract)
